<%#
    A new album, at /blog-management/masonry/.

    The gallery layout with nothing in it — the same container, the same
    classes, the same measure a published album has — because an album being
    composed and an album being read are the same page in two states.

    The shell renders for everybody. It is empty until the Worker releases a
    ticket, and what may be written is the repository's decision, not this
    template's.
%>
<div class="page-template-container">
	<div class="ed-gate">
		<%- partial('components/access-probe', { text: __('editor.checking') }) %>
	</div>

	<%# Contenteditable is put on by the editor, not here: the heading is the
	    album's name, and on a published album it is the same element. %>
	<h1 class="page-title-header"></h1>

	<%# `data-album-new` is what tells the editor there is nothing to look up —
	    arriving here IS the press, exactly as it is on /blog-management/write/. %>
	<div id="masonry-container" class="markdown-body" data-album-new="1"></div>
</div>
